Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 11:42:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 179/307] fix: energy conserving LPV propagation (Kaplanyan
 face solid angles)

First test of GV occlusion + sky light showed no visible effect. Root
cause of all three symptoms: the cone90 SH-dot propagation transferred
only ~10% of the energy per cell step (aligned transfer 0.102), which is
also why r_LPVIntensity needed to be ~150. Sky light decayed to ~1% two
cells past a doorway, and the energy the GV occlusion intercepted was
negligible to begin with. (Outdoors the deferred ambient already applies
1.0 x GetSkyColor via ClipVolumes, so the LPV sky term is inherently an
interior feature.)

- Propagation now reprojects each neighbour's flux through the five
  faces of the destination cell weighted by their real solid angles
  (far 0.4007 sr, side 0.4234 sr) and deposits cosine lobes around the
  face normals. The 5 faces of all 6 neighbours partition the sphere:
  ~0.9 total transfer per step, isotropic fields survive (~89%/step vs
  ~1% before).
- Defaults rescaled: r_LPVIntensity 150 -> 5, r_LPVSecondaryBounce
  2.0 -> 0.25 (the conserving operator feeds the feedback loop much
  harder). All previous tuning is invalidated.
- r_LPVDebug 1 now logs the GV blocking potential per surfel and the
  sky colour/premult for input validation.

